WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.499 --> 00:00:17.961
duke's secretary spoke immediately after the introductions.

2
00:00:17.981 --> 00:00:21.384
"I called this morning to prevent you from going to London.

3
00:00:21.844 --> 00:00:22.945
It seems I was too late.

4
00:00:23.285 --> 00:00:26.768
His Grace is surprised that you have taken such steps without his consultation."

5
00:00:28.049 --> 00:00:31.092
"When I learned the police had failed began the headmaster.

6
00:00:32.192 --> 00:00:36.094
"His Grace is not convinced that they have," interrupted the secretary.

7
00:00:36.734 --> 00:00:41.696
The headmaster tried to plead his case, but the secretary kept insisting that the duke was extremely displeased.

8
00:00:42.297 --> 00:00:45.778
Finally the headmaster said, "There is a solution; Mr.

9
00:00:45.818 --> 00:00:47.659
Holmes can return on the train tomorrow."

10
00:00:48.559 --> 00:00:51.601
"Hardly," said Holmes in his laziest voice.

11
00:00:51.621 --> 00:00:53.742
"I think I'll hike your moors.

12
00:00:54.442 --> 00:00:58.364
The only question is: will you allow us to stay here or shall we take a room at

13
00:00:58.404 --> 00:00:59.004
the village inn?"

14
00:01:00.064 --> 00:01:03.947
The unfortunate headmaster looked as if he was about to jump off a cliff, when the duke's deep

15
00:01:03.987 --> 00:01:06.188
voice said, "I agree with Mr.

16
00:01:06.249 --> 00:01:08.370
Wilder, that you should have consulted with me.

17
00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:10.051
But, since Mr.

18
00:01:10.111 --> 00:01:14.895
Holmes seems interested in the case whether he is wanted here or not, he ought to stay with

19
00:01:14.935 --> 00:01:15.995
me at Holdernesse Hall."

20
00:01:16.015 --> 00:01:19.798
"I thank your Grace," said Holmes humbly.

21
00:01:19.818 --> 00:01:24.702
"But for the purposes of my investigation, I should remain here at the school."

22
00:01:24.722 --> 00:01:27.824
"As you like," responded the duke.

23
00:01:28.616 --> 00:01:31.897
"My secretary and I are happy to provide you with any information."

24
00:01:31.917 --> 00:01:36.218
"I may need to speak with you at the Hall," said Holmes.

25
00:01:37.098 --> 00:01:42.540
"For now, however, I was just wondering whether you have made up any explanation for the disappearance of

26
00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:43.020
your son?"

27
00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:45.841
"I have not," said the duke.

28
00:01:46.781 --> 00:01:51.802
"Sorry, if this is uncomfortable, but I have to know: do you think the duchess had anything to

29
00:01:51.842 --> 00:01:52.242
do with it?"

30
00:01:52.962 --> 00:01:53.923
asked Holmes politely.

31
00:01:54.483 --> 00:01:58.344
The duke hesitated, and then replied, "I do not think so."

32
00:01:59.328 --> 00:02:03.310
"The other obvious explanation is kidnapping for ransom," continued Holmes.

33
00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:06.372
"Have you received any kind of ransom demand?"

34
00:02:07.232 --> 00:02:08.713
"No," said the duke.

35
00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:11.895
"Last question, your Grace," said Holmes.

36
00:02:11.915 --> 00:02:15.076
"I know you wrote to your son on the last day of his disappearance.

37
00:02:15.557 --> 00:02:17.818
Was there anything in the letter that may have upset him?"

38
00:02:18.578 --> 00:02:21.440
"No, certainly not," said the duke abruptly.

39
00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:23.621
"Did you post the letter yourself?"

40
00:02:24.201 --> 00:02:24.962
continued Holmes.

41
00:02:25.782 --> 00:02:29.104
The answer to Holmes' question came not from the duke but from his secretary.

42
00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:33.577
"His Grace does not post his own letters," said the secretary angrily.

43
00:02:33.597 --> 00:02:35.238
"I post all his letters."

44
00:02:35.258 --> 00:02:38.178
"Are you sure you posted the one in question?"

45
00:02:38.899 --> 00:02:39.419
asked Holmes.

46
00:02:39.439 --> 00:02:41.840
"Yes," replied the secretary.

47
00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:42.860
"I observed it."

48
00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:46.441
"How many letters does your Grace usually write each day?"

49
00:02:47.341 --> 00:02:47.901
asked Holmes.

50
00:02:48.822 --> 00:02:50.842
"Twenty to thirty," answered the duke.

51
00:02:50.862 --> 00:02:53.183
"But surely this is irrelevant.

52
00:02:53.523 --> 00:02:56.564
I have advised the police to continue their search in the south of France.

53
00:02:57.076 --> 00:03:02.661
Although I do not think my wife is involved, the boy may have had some wrongheaded notion—no doubt

54
00:03:02.881 --> 00:03:04.122
aided by that German teacher.

55
00:03:04.863 --> 00:03:06.184
If you discover anything, Mr.

56
00:03:06.224 --> 00:03:08.105
Holmes, contact me at the Hall."

57
00:03:08.966 --> 00:03:13.030
It seemed Holmes had more questions, but the duke's abrupt manner ended the interview.

58
00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:18.794
The doorman had barely closed the door after the duke and his secretary, when Holmes energetically began his

59
00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:24.239
investigation. Holmes searched the rooms of the boy and the German teacher, but they revealed nothing further.

60
00:03:25.324 --> 00:03:28.886
Next Holmes left the school and came back an hour later with a large map of the local

61
00:03:28.966 --> 00:03:33.969
area. "Watson, geography is the key to this mystery," said Holmes.

62
00:03:35.109 --> 00:03:38.371
I helped him lay the map out, and then we began to examine it.

63
00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:42.273
Holmes put a colored pin into the map where the Priory School was located.

64
00:03:43.134 --> 00:03:44.895
"Look here," said Holmes.

65
00:03:44.915 --> 00:03:48.617
"Here's the main road running east and west past the school.

66
00:03:49.357 --> 00:03:52.539
Please note that there is no side road for a mile either way.

67
00:03:53.239 --> 00:03:55.773
If they went by road, it had to be this road."

68
00:03:56.714 --> 00:03:59.276
Holmes then said he doubted if they had taken the road.

69
00:03:59.957 --> 00:04:04.140
After he had obtained the map, he had talked to a constable on duty near the eastern side

70
00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:09.725
road. The constable swore that he had seen no one that night, and Holmes commented that he was

71
00:04:09.765 --> 00:04:10.986
a very reliable witness.

72
00:04:11.887 --> 00:04:15.170
Holmes' second conversation had been with the landlady of the Red Bull inn.

73
00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:20.074
On the night in question, she had been ill and so she had sent for the doctor.

74
00:04:20.594 --> 00:04:24.793
Her son had waited for the doctor until morning, and the boy had sworn he saw no one

75
00:04:24.853 --> 00:04:25.834
on the road all night.

76
00:04:26.554 --> 00:04:31.057
If the combined testimonies were accurate, it meant the fugitives had not taken the road.

77
00:04:31.717 --> 00:04:35.219
I thought the testimonies to be reliable, so I agreed with Holmes' deductions.

78
00:04:35.239 --> 00:04:39.922
"These testimonies suggest that a different route was taken," said Holmes.

79
00:04:39.942 --> 00:04:42.463
"But the bicycle," I said.

80
00:04:42.483 --> 00:04:45.885
"A good cyclist doesn't need a road," said Holmes.

81
00:04:45.905 --> 00:04:50.288
"Besides, the moor is intersected with paths, and the moon was full."

82
00:04:51.208 --> 00:04:54.971
Suddenly there was an agitated knock on our door, and the door burst open.

83
00:04:54.991 --> 00:04:58.793
"At last we have a clue," exclaimed the headmaster.

84
00:04:58.813 --> 00:05:03.276
"The boy's cap has been found with a bunch of Gypsies who had been camping on the moor.

85
00:05:03.776 --> 00:05:06.618
They say they found it on the moor, but the police are not convinced.

86
00:05:07.299 --> 00:05:09.780
I guess we're not going to need your services after all."

87
00:05:10.721 --> 00:05:15.624
Holmes acknowledged that finding the cap was indeed good news, but he didn't think the Gypsies were involved.

88
00:05:16.105 --> 00:05:19.167
The headmaster assured us that the police had it under control.

89
00:05:20.167 --> 00:05:22.480
The next morning, Holmes and I started out early.

90
00:05:23.041 --> 00:05:27.582
Holmes said we should head toward the area of the moor that was marshy, because there may be

91
00:05:27.642 --> 00:05:28.182
tracks there.

92
00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:33.843
For most of the morning, the only tracks we found were those of sheep and cows, but then

93
00:05:33.943 --> 00:05:37.124
at midday we came to something that was certainly a bicycle track.

94
00:05:37.885 --> 00:05:40.045
I shouted for joy, but Homes calmed me.

95
00:05:40.065 --> 00:05:44.146
"Indeed a bicycle tire, but not the German teacher's bicycle.

96
00:05:44.706 --> 00:05:50.328
These tire tracks are made by a patched set of Dunlop tires; the bicycle we want has Palmer

97
00:05:50.368 --> 00:05:55.272
tires." I wondered if it was the boy's bicycle, but Holmes seemed to think not.

98
00:05:55.872 --> 00:06:00.497
Nonetheless, he was curious so we decided to follow the bicycle tracks back in the direction of the

99
00:06:00.538 --> 00:06:00.838
school.
